{%- comment -%}
  WHAT IT IS: the page's plain-language intro.

  Was a problem/agitation block living inside the hero section: a negative is orange, the light
  falls off, the roll drifts. Anyone shopping for conversion software already knows all of that,
  so restating it spent the best slot on the page telling the reader something they came in
  knowing. This says what toneScan Studio is and what it does instead.

  Split out of the hero into its own section so other sections can be ordered in front of it.
  Page-wide CSS and JS are rendered once by layout/tonescan.liquid, so this file carries markup
  only and can be reordered or removed without taking them with it.

  Deliberately uncarded. The bento is a grid of boxes and the feature list is an accordion, so a
  third boxed grid here would read as more of the same.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="tonescan-landing tw:text-neutral-200">
  {%- comment -%} Screenshots live in Shopify Files (Content > Files). {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign ts_cdn = 'https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0634/3199/9736/files' -%}

  <section class="ts-intro">
    <div class="ts-intro__inner">
      <div class="ts-intro__head">
        <h2 class="ts-intro__title">One application for your complete workflow.</h2>
        <div class="ts-intro__lead">
          <p>toneScan Studio is standalone software that brings lab-grade speed and&nbsp;accuracy to camera scanning.</p>
          <p>The conversion works from how film and&nbsp;paper actually behave rather than a look someone drew by eye, so the colour is right before you touch a single slider.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ul class="ts-intro__pillars">
        <li class="ts-intro__pillar">
          <span class="ts-intro__pbg" aria-hidden="true" style="--shot:url('{{ ts_cdn }}/organise.png')"></span>
          <span class="ts-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 2 2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5Z"/><path d="M2 17l10 5 10-5"/><path d="M2 12l10 5 10-5"/></svg></span>
          <h3 class="ts-intro__plabel">All of it in one app</h3>
          <p class="ts-intro__ptext">Catalogue, convert, correct, calibrate and&nbsp;export your scans. toneScan Studio is the new home for your whole film photography workflow.</p>
          <a class="ts-intro__pcta" href="#features">See what it does <span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span></a>
        </li>
        <li class="ts-intro__pillar">
          <span class="ts-intro__pbg" aria-hidden="true" style="--shot:url('{{ ts_cdn }}/rgb-merge.png')"></span>
          <span class="ts-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="9" cy="9.5" r="5.2"/><circle cx="15" cy="9.5" r="5.2"/><circle cx="12" cy="15" r="5.2"/></svg></span>
          <h3 class="ts-intro__plabel">Trichromatic scanning</h3>
          <p class="ts-intro__ptext">Get the colour lab scanners are known for: cleaner from the start, less to fix afterwards, and&nbsp;shadows that hold together.</p>
          <a class="ts-intro__pcta" href="#rgb">How RGB works <span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span></a>
        </li>
        <li class="ts-intro__pillar">
          <span class="ts-intro__pbg" aria-hidden="true" style="--shot:url('{{ ts_cdn }}/pixel-preview.png')"></span>
          <span class="ts-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M13 2 4 14h6l-1 8 9-12h-6l1-8Z"/></svg></span>
          <h3 class="ts-intro__plabel">Fast, and&nbsp;stays out of the way</h3>
          <p class="ts-intro__ptext">Quick imports, a GPU viewport, and&nbsp;an interface that answers instantly. Keyboard shortcuts let you fly through a roll like a lab tech.</p>
          <a class="ts-intro__pcta" href="#how-it-works">See it in use <span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span></a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

